Well, I'd see it the other way round; pudding farming is worse than
anything else related to object generation (including wishes). (Fix
the farming exploit and those rare wishes are no real issue any more;
in my book.)

Generally there seems to be the assumption that victory or fate are
primarily determined by objects. And it is certainly (and trivially)
true that the presence (or absence) of objects will influence your
chances, occasionally even significantly. You may get an early wish,
wish for reflection and get killed by a poisonous arrow or pit, or
wish for poison resistance and get killed by the wand of death (or
some "less effective" attack; objects are no solution to survive,
they are the vehicles to support you and they are highly depending
on the actual evolution of the specific game. Once at the Castle
(where the "offensive" wand is located) folks often even don't need
any wishes any more to proceed, or need it only for convenience. It
depends.

There are few properties "necessary" to survive; and you don't need
wishes for objects to obtain those properties. But if you happen to
get a wish (or even a couple wishes), fine; wishes are a shortcut to
acquire something that might not even be generated (currently or in
the whole game). But wishes are far from a guarantee to survive even
the next level.

(Oh, I fear I digressed a bit; my rant would have been better placed
as answer to another posting in this thread.)

